course: dictionary
lesson: 7222
title: Photo and photograph
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A photo is a picture taken with a camera or a phone. Photo is short for photograph, so the two words mean the same thing. When you meet photo in a sentence, ask yourself: is this a picture someone took? «Take a photo» and «a photo album» use the word in the same way.
explain: The words around a photo give you clues. «A blurry or faraway photo is not real proof.» Blurry means not clear, so a photo that is hard to see may not show the truth.
explain: Photos can be changed. «Many online photos are filtered or edited» means they have been made to look different from real life. «The famous 1934 Loch Ness monster photo was a fake made with a toy» shows that a photo can be a trick, so check before you believe one.
explain: Think before you share. «A girl in Florida posted a photo in her school uniform with her street in the background.» A stranger used the clues in that photo to find out where she lived. A photo can show more than you mean it to, so ask a trusted adult before you share one.
fact: A photo is a picture taken with a camera or a phone.
fact: Photo is short for photograph.
fact: Photos are used in school, on holidays and in photo albums, and in maths you can count them or work out how many fit on a page.
fact: Before you take or share someone's photo, ask them first.
fact: Do not share photos online with strangers, because a photo can show clues about where you live or go to school.
exercise: What is a photo? | A song played on the radio | *A picture taken with a camera or a phone | A drawing made with pencils | A type of train
exercise: «A blurry or faraway photo is not real proof.» What does blurry mean? | Brand new | *Not clear, hard to see | Printed in colour | Very bright and shiny
exercise: Photo is short for which longer word? | *Photograph | Telephone | Photosynthesis | Photocopy
test: «Many online photos are filtered or edited.» What does edited mean here? | *Changed to look different from real life | Deleted from the phone | Sent to a friend | Printed on paper
test: You want to share a photo of your friend online. What should you do first? | *Ask your friend and a trusted adult first | Send it to a stranger to be safe | Post it straight away so everyone can see | Add her home address to the caption
exam: Why did the stranger find out where the girl in Florida lived? | Her parents posted a photo of the police |  | The photo was edited to look like a toy | *Her school uniform and street in the background were clues in the photo | Her photo was blurry and faraway
